`Environment` carries the session's `PersistentState`; `SessionApp` builds the environment once and hands it to the emitter. A view obtains its signals from `env.state()` inside `render(...)` — no constructor args. `PersistentState.signal(name, initial)` memoizes by name, so repeat calls return the same signal (stable identity).

